title: 'cumulus: refactor slot based builder loop'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: "### Description\n\nFirst PR of a stack extracted from #12537 (resubmissions\
    \ support).\n\nRefactor (no behavior change). `run_block_builder`'s monolithic\
    \ loop is split into phases so later work can plug in per phase:\n\n- `BuilderEnv`\
    \ groups the clients, caches, and per-task state; the loop body shrinks to prepare_slot\
    \ \u2192 plan_cores \u2192 per-core build.\n- `prepare_slot` resolves everything\
    \ for one slot iteration up to a successful slot claim, returned as `SlotContext`;\
    \ `plan_cores` resolves the claim queue into a `CorePlan` (cores and per-core\
    \ block counts).\n- Small extractions along the way: `SchedulingParams::at` and\
    \ `ParentSearchParams::new` constructors, `included_header_at_execution` and `allowed_pov_size`\
    \ helpers, `update_backing_connections` (which now logs a previously silent authorities()\
    \ failure), `claim_queue_offset` and redundant header/hash fields dropped from\
    \ the context structs.\n\nOne behavior fix (second commit). The two-phase context\
    \ derivation reuses the parent search result when the build parent's runtime disagrees\
    \ with the para best's. If the search ran with V3 params and the re-derive settled\
    \ on V2, the reused included_at_scheduling snapshot was taken at a V3 scheduling\
    \ parent and could be stale for the V2 execution context. The V2 arm now re-fetches\
    \ the included head at its relay parent in that case (search_ran_v3 flag); the\
    \ reverse direction is expected/assumed to not occur, since a V3 \u2192 V2 parachain\
    \ rollback is not supported, and the plan is to not end up needing it, by testing\
    \ V3 parachains before recommending it officially."
crates:
- name: cumulus-client-consensus-aura
  bump: patch
- name: cumulus-client-consensus-common
  bump: patch
